<%# locals: (title:, id:, body_class: nil) %>
<%# A titled card holding one group of common/checkbox_row boxes, for a long
    checklist filed in groups. Rendered with `render layout:`: the caller's
    block is the rows. Not common/checkbox_tile, which is the bordered box
    around a single checkbox.

    The title names the group for a screen reader (role="group"), which is
    what says whose "Interface" a box is when its rows carry short labels. It
    is an <h4>, one level under the subheading the cards sit beneath. Not a
    <fieldset>: components/forms.css gives every fieldset inside a form the
    blue rule and gradient of f.fieldset.

    The card carries no spacing of its own: the wrapper that flows the cards
    sets the gap under each and keeps one from splitting across two columns
    (teams_positions/_role_grants). id: is the heading's id and has to be
    unique on the page. body_class: lays the rows out, as "grid grid-cols-2"
    does for a card of short labels. %>
<%= ui_card shadow: :none, role: "group", aria: { labelledby: id } do %>
  <h4 id="<%= id %>" class="heading-title text-heading px-3 py-2 border-b border-line"><%= title %></h4>
  <div class="<%= class_names("px-2 py-1", body_class) %>"><%= yield %></div>
<% end %>
